    "https://univofky.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/UKSS/job/UKKD---Main-Campus/Distribution-Assistant-Associate_R-000004577": {
      "title": "Distribution Assistant Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: Distribution Assistant Associate Requisition Number: R-000004577 Department Name: Inventory and Logistics Work Location: UKKD - Main Campus Grade Level: 1 Type of Position: Regular Position Time Status: Full time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Day (United States of America) Job Description: Job Summary \r\n Performs activities related to the distribution of equipment and supplies, following established procedures and under the guidance of a supervisor. Maintains accurate stock records and supports inventory integrity across assigned areas, including monitoring consumption and assisting with reorder and replenishment requirements. Supports proper organization in adherence with regulatory, safety, and organizational standards. Assists team members in fulfillment and distribution of supplies, escalating issues as needed. \r\n \r\n Essential Functions \r\n • Fulfills orders and issues supplies from inventory, distribution partners and vendor direct orders to appropriate departments, following established procedures and under supervision, ensuring accuracy and timeliness. Examines stock for conformance to specifications and reports discrepancies to supervisor. ​ \r\n • Unpacks, organizes, and stores materials in designated locations based on storage requirements, considering factors such as temperature, humidity, and safety protocols. \r\n • Transports materials between receiving docks, storage areas, and user departments, maintaining records of material movement. \r\n • Assists in monitoring and replenishing inventory levels in designated areas, escalating discrepancies or shortages to supervisor to ensure compliance with regulatory standards and organizational policy. \r\n • Maintains cleanliness and organization of storage areas, including removal of waste and dusting of shelves following standard procedures and safety guidelines. \r\n • Performs other duties as assigned. \r\n \r\n Education Requirement \r\n High school diploma or equivalent experience \r\n \r\n Experience Requirement \r\n 0-2 years of experience in a healthcare, clinical setting, or a relevant area \r\n An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. All experience must be paid and in the same related field. Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week. Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted. \r\n \r\n Certifications & Licensures \r\n Valid Driver’s license \r\n \r\n Working Conditions \r\n A. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) \r\n B. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n C. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs: 4. Regular (> 50% of the time) \r\n D. Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs: 4. Regular (> 50% of the time) \r\n E. Sitting at computer workstation for extended periods: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n F. Risk of back injury from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n G. Repetitive motion: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) \r\n H. Working at heights above 4 feet: 1. Never \r\n I. Working in confined spaces: 1. Never \r\n J. Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n K. Job-related travel: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n L. Loud noises: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n M. Temperature extremes: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n N. Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n O. Radiation: 1. Never \r\n P. Burns: 1. Never \r\n Q. Cuts/Punctures: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n R. Bloodborne/airborne pathogens: 1. Never \r\n S. Recombinant DNA or viral vectors: 1. Never \r\n T. Combative/violent people: 1. Never \r\n U. Animal handling (including carcasses): 1. Never \r\n V. Please specify other(s) and amount of exposure (i.e. Occasional, Intermittent or Regular): N/A \r\n \r\n Physical Demands \r\n This position requires regular standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; regular standing or walking with objects up to 25 pounds; intermittent lifting, pushing, and/or pulling of objects weighing up to 50 pounds; and occasional lifting, pushing, and/or pulling of objects over 50 pounds. Also involves occasional sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time; performing tasks with intermittent repetitive motions; occasional risk of back injury from moving or lifting equipment or materials; occasional risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job; and occasional exposure to hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, cuts/punctures, loud noises, temperature extremes, and job-related travel. \r\n Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
    },
    "https://univofky.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/UKSS/job/Joe-Craft-Center/HR-Business-Associate_R-000004057-1": {
      "title": "HR Business Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: HR Business Associate Requisition Number: R-000004057 Department Name: Business Partners Work Location: Joe Craft Center Grade Level: 2 Type of Position: Regular Position Time Status: Full time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Day (United States of America) Job Description: Job Summary Responsible for providing administrative payroll and human resources support for the Athletics Department, for processing payroll activities, monitoring employee time entry and approvals, coordinating payroll actions, supporting hiring processes for student and temporary employees and ensuring accurate and timely compensation for Athletics personnel. Serves as a resource for payroll procedures, timekeeping practices, and employment transactions while providing support for operational and compliance requirements. All University of Kentucky Athletics Department employees are required to conduct themselves in accordance with the rules, regulations, and policies of the National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA), the College Sports Commission (CSC), the Southeastern Conference (SEC), the University, and any other applicable regulatory body. Essential Functions • Monitors time for employees in a dual system role using UKG and SAP systems. • Monitors and enters time for Stat Crew members, Events and Hospitality Staff, Hourly Staff, and Students in both the UKG system and SAP system to ensure Workers are paid correctly and in a timely manner. • Prepares and sends out bi-weekly notifications to all staff with time-entry and payroll reminders. • Processes all payroll actions for UK athletics to ensure all policies and procedures are followed, and employees are paid correctly and in a timely manner. • Proactively monitors time approval screens in SAP as well as timecards in UKG during payroll, reminding managers to approve time, research and reconcile payroll discrepancies prior to the approval process. Oversees and resolves all payroll issues from employees and students regarding payroll policies, payroll time, and payroll procedures. • Completes PARs for student new hires, rehires, pay adjustments, additional assignments and end of assignment actions. • Manages hiring, pay adjustments, separations for temporary employees in Workday. • Creates separation actions in a timely manner in both systems to ensure up-to-date and accurate employee records. • Assists in completing I-9's for new staff and temporary hires in Workday. • Assists business office with payroll sorting at the end of each pay period to assist with monthly budget reconciliation. • Assist business office with entering employee taxable information before payroll deadlines. • Provides daily administrative support to Student-Athlete Services staff, including academic counselors, tutors, and program leadership, and serves as a primary point of contact for facility operations and visitor engagement. • Coordinates front-facing operations within the CATS facility, managing high-volume interactions with student-athletes, staff, recruits, families, and visitors while ensuring a professional and organized environment. • Supports operational needs including monitoring office supplies, coordinating room reservations, and assisting with maintenance and functionality of office equipment and systems. • Assists with student-athlete support processes, including scholarship check distribution, tracking attendance and fines related to tutor sessions, and preparing student organizational materials. • Provides support for tutor and mentor programs, including assisting with scheduling, reporting, and backup coordination in the absence of program leadership. • Coordinates ordering, distribution, and tracking of required course materials for student-athletes and tutors, including managing purchases, maintaining records, and supporting compliance-related documentation. • Processes tutor and mentor payroll documentation, including reviewing submitted hours, identifying discrepancies, and ensuring accurate and timely payroll support. • Supports student-athlete programming and events, including coordination of workshops, recognition programs, and departmental initiatives, and assists with research and reporting on academic or program related topics. • Performs other duties as assigned. Education Requirement Bachelor's Degree required. Experience Requirement 2 years of experience in human resources, payroll administration, business operations, accounting, finance, personnel administration, or a related field. Experience processing payroll transactions and utilizing HRIS, payroll, or timekeeping systems preferred. Experience with SAP, Workday, UKG, or similar enterprise systems preferred. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. All experience must be paid and in the same related field. Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week. Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted. Certifications & Licensures Professional certification in Human Resources, Payroll Administration, or a related field preferred. Working Conditions A. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs: 1. Never B. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs: 1. Never C. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) D. Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs: 1. Never E. Sitting at computer workstation for extended periods: 4. Regular (>50% of the time) F. Risk of back injury from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials: 4. Regular (>50% of the time) G. Repetitive motion: 4. Regular (>50% of the time) H. Working at heights above 4 feet: 1. Never I . Working in confined spaces: 1. Never J. Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job: 1. Never K. Job-related travel: 1. Never L. Loud noises: 1. Never M. Temperature extremes: 1. Never N. Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste: 1. Never O. Radiation: 1. Never P. Burns: 1. Never Q. Cuts/Punctures: 1. Never R. Bloodborne/airborne pathogens: 1. Never S. Recombinant DNA or viral vectors: 1. Never T. Combative/violent people: 1. Never U. Animal handling (including carcasses): 1. Never V. Please specify other(s) and amount of exposure (ie. Occasional, Intermittent or Regular): None Physical Demands This position requires regular sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time and performing tasks with regular repetitive motions such as typing, data entry, payroll processing, and reviewing electronic records. Responsibilities also include intermittent standing or walking while carrying objects weighing up to 10 pounds. The position requires extensive use of payroll, human resources, and financial systems to support payroll processing, employment transactions, reporting, and record maintenance. Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
    },
    "https://univofky.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/UKSS/job/UKKD---Main-Campus/Emergency-Management-Specialist_R-000004372": {
      "title": "Emergency Management Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: Emergency Management Specialist Requisition Number: R-000004372 Department Name: Management Work Location: UKKD - Main Campus Grade Level: 6 Type of Position: Regular Position Time Status: Full time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Day (United States of America) Job Description: Job Summary \r\n Responsible for supporting the development and delivery of emergency management education and training programs. Assists in preparing instructional materials, coordinating schedules, and facilitating learning sessions related to emergency preparedness and response. Collaborates with staff and leadership to promote awareness and compliance with safety and emergency protocols. Ensures training activities align with organizational standards and regulatory requirements. \r\n \r\n Essential Functions \r\n • Assist in planning and delivering emergency management education and training programs. \r\n • Prepare instructional materials, presentations, and resources for staff education sessions. \r\n • Coordinate training schedules, attendance tracking, and documentation of participant completion. \r\n • Support emergency drills and exercises to evaluate readiness and response effectiveness. \r\n • Maintain training databases and records in compliance with regulatory and organizational requirements. \r\n • Communicate with departments to ensure understanding of emergency policies and procedures. \r\n • Provide on-site support during emergency events, drills, and evaluations as directed. \r\n • Participate in reviewing and updating emergency education content based on feedback and regulatory changes. \r\n • Collaborate with educators, safety officers, and management to enhance program quality and engagement. \r\n • Perform other duties as assigned. \r\n \r\n Education Requirement \r\n Bachelor’s degree \r\n - \r\n \r\n Experience Requirement \r\n 0-2 years of experience \r\n \r\n An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. All experience must be paid and in the same related field. Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week. Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted. \r\n \r\n Certifications & Licensures \r\n Completion of NIMS courses (IS-100, IS-200, IS-700, and IS-800) required within six months of hire. \r\n Completion of FEMA Professional Development Series and/or Professional Continuity Practitioner preferred. \r\n \r\n Working Conditions \r\n A. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n B. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs: 1. Never \r\n C. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) \r\n D. Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) \r\n E. Sitting at computer workstation for extended periods: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) \r\n F. Risk of back injury from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials: 1. Never \r\n G. Repetitive motion: 4. Regular (> 50% of the time) \r\n H. Working at heights above 4 feet: 1. Never \r\n I. Working in confined spaces: 1. Never \r\n J. Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job: 1. Never \r\n K. Job-related travel: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n L. Loud noises: 1. Never \r\n M. Temperature extremes: 1. Never \r\n N. Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste: 1. Never \r\n O. Radiation: 1. Never \r\n P. Burns: 1. Never \r\n Q. Cuts/Punctures: 1. Never \r\n R. Bloodborne/airborne pathogens: 1. Never \r\n S. Recombinant DNA or viral vectors: 1. Never \r\n T. Combative/violent people: 1. Never \r\n U. Animal handling (including carcasses): 1. Never \r\n V. Please specify other(s) and amount of exposure (i.e. Occasional, Intermittent or Regular): N/A \r\n \r\n Physical Demands \r\n This position requires frequent maintenance of a stationary posture behind a computer or while presenting to individuals or groups; frequent mobility throughout the Medical Center or while rounding; and constant communication with people electronically, by phone, and in-person. The role also demands constant operation of a computer and telephone; constant lifting and/or moving of up to 15 pounds and frequent lifting and/or moving of up to 25 pounds, with occasional lifting and/or moving of up to 50 pounds. Specific vision abilities—including close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, and depth perception—are also required. Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
    },
    "https://univofky.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/UKSS/job/Pavilion/Payroll-Settlement-Coordinator_R-000004535-2": {
      "title": "Payroll Settlement Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: Payroll Settlement Coordinator Requisition Number: R-000004535 Department Name: Shared Services Work Location: Pavilion Grade Level: 4 Type of Position: Regular Position Time Status: Full time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Day (United States of America) Job Description: Job Summary Responsible for settling expense, third party payroll, and on cycle and on demand payroll runs, maintaining accurate vendor payment records, and ensuring timely, accurate payment for all deduction recipients. Independently processes payroll deduction data, ensures compliance, provides guidance, and supports process improvements. Collaborates with HR, Payroll, Accounts Payable, and management to resolve vendor issues, support financial reporting and audit activities, and ensures compliance with organizational policies in day-to-day operations. Essential Functions • Maintain and process all third party payroll, garnishment systems in compliance with organizational policies and standards. • Assist with generating government payments like taxes, unemployment, and child support. • Compile, process, and audit payroll data, including quick charge, deductions, garnishments, levies, direct deposits, and manual corrections; settling all runs promptly and accurately. • Prepare and payroll vendor reports, including routine, ad hoc, and compliance reporting • Update, maintain, and communicate policies and guidelines related to garnishments, quick charge, and third party payments as necessary • Serve as a resource to system users; independently troubleshoot and resolve payroll deduction and vendor reconciliation and escalating highly complex matters. • Ensure compliance with payroll laws, regulations, and organizational policies. • Collaborate with HR, staffing, vendors, and management teams to ensure payroll accuracy and resolve issues. • • Recommend and implement process improvements to enhance timekeeping and payroll accuracy, compliance, and efficiency. • Performs other duties as assigned. Education Requirement High school diploma or equivalent experience Experience Requirement 5 years of experience in finance, accounting, healthcare, clinical setting, or a relevant area An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. All experience must be paid and in the same related field. Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week. Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted. Certifications & Licensures N/A Working Conditions A. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) B. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs: 1. Never C. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) D. Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) E. Sitting at computer workstation for extended periods: 4. Regular (> 50% of the time) F. Risk of back injury from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials: 1. Never G. Repetitive motion: 4. Regular (> 50% of the time) H. Working at heights above 4 feet: 1. Never I. Working in confined spaces: 1. Never J. Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job: 1. Never K. Job-related travel: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) L. Loud noises: 1. Never M. Temperature extremes: 1. Never N. Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste: 1. Never O. Radiation: 1. Never P. Burns: 1. Never Q. Cuts/Punctures: 1. Never R. Bloodborne/airborne pathogens: 1. Never S. Recombinant DNA or viral vectors: 1. Never T. Combative/violent people: 1. Never U. Animal handling (including carcasses): 1. Never V. Please specify other(s) and amount of exposure (i.e. Occasional, Intermittent or Regular): N/A Physical Demands This position requires regular sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time; performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); intermittent standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; occasional standing or walking with objects up to 25 pounds; and occasional lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to 50 pounds. Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
