      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: Patient Registration Representative Requisition Number: R-000004539 Department Name: Patient Registration Work Location: UK Chandler Hospital, Pavilion A Grade Level: 3 Type of Position: PRN Position Time Status: Part time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Flex (United States of America) Job Description: Job Summary \r\n Responsible for ensuring accuracy and completeness of patient registration and billing data after the clinical encounter. Provides expertise in reviewing, correcting, and submitting claims to support timely and accurate reimbursement. Coordinates with patients, payers, and internal departments to collect missing information, resolve data errors, and reduce denials. Contributes to process improvements, mentors staff and supports revenue cycle performance by maintaining compliance with organizational policies and regulatory standards. \r\n \r\n Essential Functions \r\n • Maintains a queue or worklist of accounts flagged for registration or billing follow-up. \r\n • Independently review and correct claims and charge errors rejected, denied, or suspended due to registration or data issues. \r\n • Contacts patients to collect or clarify workers’ compensation, accident, or insurance details including claim numbers, employer, or authorization information. \r\n • Documents communications, tracks responses, and updates patient account records with accuracy. \r\n • Coordinates with employers, insurance carriers, attorneys, or adjusters to obtain required documentation. \r\n • Verifies and obtains subrogation or third-party liability information to support accurate billing. \r\n • Meets departmental KPIs for claim resolution, registration completeness, denial reduction, and accounts receivable performance. \r\n • Collaborates with registration, billing, clinical, coding, and customer service teams to ensure seamless information flow. \r\n • Provides feedback to frontline registration staff to reduce recurring data entry errors. \r\n • Participates in process improvement initiatives to enhance registration and billing accuracy. \r\n • Performs other duties as assigned. \r\n \r\n Education Requirement: High school diploma or equivalent \r\n \r\n Experience Requirement: 2–3 years of experience in patient access, registration, billing, or revenue cycle operations \r\n An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. All experience must be paid and in the same related field. Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week. Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted. \r\n \r\n Certifications & Licensures: N/A \r\n \r\n Working Conditions \r\n A. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs: 1. Intermittent (10%-50%). \r\n B. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs: 1. Never. \r\n C. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs: 3. Intermittent (10%–50%). \r\n D. Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs: 1. Never to 2. Occasional (not a regular expectation). \r\n E. Sitting at computer workstation for extended periods: 4. Intermittent (10%-50%). \r\n F. Risk of back injury from moving, lifting, or positioning patients, equipment, or materials: 1. Never. \r\n G. Repetitive motion: 4. Regular (> 50% of the time) (typing, data entry, scanning). \r\n H. Working at heights above 4 feet: 1. Never. \r\n I. Working in confined spaces: 1. Never. \r\n J. Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job: 1. Rare. \r\n K. Job-related travel: 1. Never to 2. Occasional. \r\n L. Loud noises: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time). \r\n M. Temperature extremes: 1. Never. \r\n N. Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time). \r\n O. Radiation: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time). \r\n P. Burns: 1. Never. \r\n Q. Cuts/Punctures: 1. Never to 2. Occasional \r\n R. Bloodborne/airborne pathogens: 3. Intermittent (10%–50%). \r\n S. Recombinant DNA or viral vectors: 1. Never. \r\n T. Combative/violent people: 3. Intermittent (10%–50%). \r\n U. Animal handling (including carcasses): 1. Never. \r\n V. Please specify others: Exposure to communicable diseases. High-stress environment, frequent patient/family interactions, and potential exposure to traumatic situations. \r\n \r\n Physical Demands \r\n This position requires intermittent sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time; performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); intermittent standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; occasional standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds; and occasional lifting, pushing, or pulling objects weighing up to 50 pounds. The role also involves frequent standing while performing tasks and frequent walking throughout the work environment. Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
    },
    "https://univofky.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/UKSS/job/Frank-D-Peterson-Service-Bldg/Endpoint-Engineer_R-000004660": {
      "title": "Endpoint Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: Endpoint Engineer Requisition Number: R-000004660 Department Name: Field & End User Services Work Location: Frank D. Peterson Service Bldg Grade Level: 5 Type of Position: Regular Position Time Status: Full time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Day (United States of America) Job Description: Job Summary \n\n Responsible for delivering Tier 1 and 2 technical support and ensuring reliable performance of end-user computing systems. Installs, configures, and maintains desktop operating systems, applications, and peripherals. Ensures compliance with IT standards, policies, and security requirements. Participates in IT projects, analyzes recurring issues, and contributes to process improvements. Coordinates with IT teams, vendors, and users to resolve incidents and support initiatives. \n\n \n\n Essential Functions \n\n • Prioritizes and responds to incidents, requests, and projects in alignment with SLAs. \n\n • Resolves technical issues for hardware, software, and peripherals, escalating complex issues as needed. \n\n • Installs, configures, and maintains end-user devices and applications, ensuring compliance with IT security standards. \n\n • Documents recurring issues and contributes to corrective actions. \n\n • Communicates effectively with users, team members, and vendors. \n\n • Participates in IT projects, migrations, and upgrades to meet objectives. \n\n • Identifies workflow and process improvement opportunities. \n\n • Maintains documentation in ticketing and knowledge systems. \n\n • Performs other duties as assigned. \n\n \n\n Education Requirement: Bachelor’s degree \n\n \n\n Experience Requirement: 2+ years of experience. \n\n An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. All experience must be paid and in the same related field. Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week. Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted. \n\n \n\n Certifications & Licensures: Windows 10 or Microsoft 365 Certified \n\n \n\n Working Conditions \n\n A. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \n\n B. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs: 1. Never \n\n C. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \n\n D. Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs: 1. Never \n\n E. Sitting at computer workstation for extended periods: 4. Regular (> 50% of the time) \n\n F. Risk of back injury from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials: 1. Never \n\n G. Repetitive motion: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) \n\n H. Working at heights above 4 feet: 1. Never \n\n I. Working in confined spaces: 1. Never \n\n J. Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job: 1. Never \n\n K. Job-related travel: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \n\n L. Loud noises: 1. Never \n\n M. Temperature extremes: 1. Never \n\n N. Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste: 1. Never \n\n O. Radiation: 1. Never \n\n P. Burns: 1. Never \n\n Q. Cuts/Punctures: 1. Never \n\n R. Bloodborne/airborne pathogens: 1. Never \n\n S. Recombinant DNA or viral vectors: 1. Never \n\n T. Combative/violent people: 1. Never \n\n U. Animal handling (including carcasses): 1. Never \n\n V. Please specify other(s) and amount of exposure (i.e. Occasional, Intermittent or Regular): N/A \n\n \n\n Physical Demands \n\n This position requires regular sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time; performing tasks with intermittent repetitive motion (such as typing); and occasionally standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds, as well as lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to 50 pounds. Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
