    "https://univofky.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/UKSS/job/2317-Alumni-Park-Plaza/Revenue-Cycle-Application-Analyst-Senior_R-000003712": {
      "title": "Revenue Cycle Application Analyst Senior",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: Revenue Cycle Application Analyst Senior Requisition Number: R-000003712 Department Name: Director, Patient Access and Digital Engagement Work Location: 2317 Alumni Park Plaza Grade Level: 12 Type of Position: Regular Position Time Status: Full time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Day (United States of America) Job Description: Job Summary Responsible for advanced analysis, configuration, optimization, implementation, and support of Epic Revenue Cycle applications and associated workflows. Applies subject matter expertise in areas including scheduling, registration, authorization, billing, coding, claims management, and reimbursement to improve operational efficiency, data quality, and compliance. Partners with operational stakeholders, vendors, and technical teams to evaluate business needs, design solutions, troubleshoot complex issues, and support organizational initiatives. Contributes to system governance, testing, documentation, and continuous improvement efforts. This role is primarily focused on outpatient access including but not limited to: Epic Cadence, Referrals, Prelude, RTE and other third-party patient access technologies Essential Functions Performs advanced analysis, design, configuration, maintenance, and optimization of Epic Revenue Cycle applications and workflows. Evaluates business requirements and translates operational needs into effective system solutions. Configures and supports functionality related to patient access, scheduling, registration, authorization, billing, claims, and other revenue cycle processes. Identifies opportunities to improve workflow efficiency, data quality, automation, revenue cycle performance, and user experience. Troubleshoots and resolves complex application, workflow, and integration issues through analysis and root cause investigation. Researches Epic functionality and recommends system enhancements to address operational challenges and support organizational objectives. Monitors system performance and application usage to identify areas for optimization and improvement. Participates in application implementations, upgrades, optimizations, and enhancement projects. Assists with planning, design, build, testing, deployment, and post-implementation support activities. Develops and executes integrated, regression, and user acceptance testing for enhancements, upgrades, and new functionality. Validates configuration changes and workflow design to ensure adherence to organizational standards, operational requirements, and regulatory guidelines. Collaborates with revenue cycle leaders, operational stakeholders, IT teams, and governance groups to align system functionality with business needs. Participates in workflow analysis, requirements gathering, design sessions, and solution reviews. Communicates application impacts, proposed solutions, and system changes to stakeholders. Coordinates with Epic, vendors, and technical teams regarding upgrades, releases, integrations, and issue resolution. Supports audit, compliance, and revenue integrity initiatives through review and validation of application settings and workflows. Maintains detailed documentation including workflows, build specifications, support procedures, testing results, and change management activities. Shares knowledge, best practices, and technical expertise with team members and stakeholders. Assists with onboarding, training, and knowledge transfer activities as requested. Participates in continuous improvement efforts focused on operational efficiency, system effectiveness, financial performance, and patient experience. Performs other duties as assigned. Education Requirement : Bachelor’s degree Experience Requirement : 5+ years of experience An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. All experience must be paid and in the same related field. Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week. Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted. Certifications & Licensures: Epic Certified in relevant applications or required within 90 days of hire   Working Conditions   This position operates in a hybrid work environment, with a combination of remote work and on-site presence at healthcare facilities and corporate offices as needed. Regular interaction with clinical, operational, and technical teams is required. The role may involve occasional travel between locations, participation in after-hours support activities, and response to critical system issues outside of normal business hours. Work is primarily performed in an office setting and requires extended periods of computer use and virtual collaboration. Compliance with all organizational privacy, security, and healthcare regulations is required.  Physical Demands   This position requires regular sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time; performing tasks with repetitive motions on a regular basis; intermittent standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; occasional standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds; and occasional lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to 50 pounds.  Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
    },
    "https://univofky.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/UKSS/job/UK-Chandler-Hospital-Pavilion-A/Supervisor--Registration_R-000003854": {
      "title": "Supervisor, Registration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: Supervisor, Registration Requisition Number: R-000003854 Department Name: Manager, Patient Registration Work Location: UK Chandler Hospital, Pavilion A Grade Level: 5 Type of Position: Regular Position Time Status: Full time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Day (United States of America) Job Description: Job Summary Responsible for overseeing the daily operations of patient access and registration to ensure accuracy, efficiency, and a positive patient experience. This role provides frontline leadership for staff performing scheduling and insurance verification, while ensuring compliance with established policies, payer requirements, and regulatory standards. The Supervisor serves as a key resource for staff and patients, assisting with workflow coordination, issue resolution, and continuous improvement efforts Essential Functions • Supervise patient registration staff to ensure consistent, accurate, and timely completion of registration and access functions. • Provide coaching, training, and daily guidance to staff to promote professional growth and accountability. • Monitor staff productivity, quality, and adherence to departmental performance standards and key performance indicators (KPIs). • Assist in resolving escalated patient registration or financial clearance issues, including insurance coverage and authorization concerns. • Ensure compliance with regulatory standards, payer requirements, and organizational policies in all registration activities. • Prepare and review reports on staff performance and registration activities to identify areas for improvement. • Support initiatives to enhance patient satisfaction and improve service delivery. • Collaborate with clinical and revenue cycle teams to ensure smooth handoffs and efficient workflows. • Participate in departmental meetings, workgroups, and projects to support patient access and organizational objectives. • Performs other duties as assigned. Education Requirement: High school diploma or equivalent Experience Requirement: 0-4 years of related/progressive experience An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. All experience must be paid and in the same related field. Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week. Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted. Certifications & Licensures: N/A Working Conditions A. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs: 1. Intermittent (10%-50%). B. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs: 1. Never. C. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs: 3. Intermittent (10%–50%). D. Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs: 1. Never to 2. Occasional (not a regular expectation). E. Sitting at computer workstation for extended periods: 4. Regular (> 50% of the time). F. Risk of back injury from moving, lifting, or positioning patients, equipment, or materials: 1. Occasional < 10%. G. Repetitive motion: 4. Regular (> 50% of the time) (typing, data entry, scanning). H. Working at heights above 4 feet: 1. Never. I. Working in confined spaces: 1. Never. J. Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job: 1. Rare. K. Job-related travel: 1. Never to 2. Occasional. L. Loud noises: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time). M. Temperature extremes: 1. Never. N. Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time). O. Radiation: 2. Occasional (< 10% of the time). P. Burns: 1. Never. Q. Cuts/Punctures: 1. Never to 2. Occasional R. Bloodborne/airborne pathogens: 3. Intermittent (10%–50%). S. Recombinant DNA or viral vectors: 1. Never. T. Combative/violent people: 3. Intermittent (10%–50%). U. Animal handling (including carcasses): 1. Never. V. Please specify others: Exposure to communicable diseases. High-stress environment, frequent patient/family interactions, and potential exposure to traumatic situations. Physical Demands This position requires regular sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time; performing tasks with regular repetitive motions (such as typing); intermittent standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; and occasional lifting, pushing, and/or pulling of objects up to 50 pounds or standing or walking with objects up to 25 pounds. Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
    },
    "https://univofky.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/UKSS/job/Remote-KY/Inpatient-Clinical-Documentation-Specialist-II_R-000003831": {
      "title": "Inpatient Clinical Documentation Specialist II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: Inpatient Clinical Documentation Specialist II Requisition Number: R-000003831 Department Name: Supervisor, Inpatient Clinical Documentation Work Location: Remote-KY Grade Level: 11 Type of Position: Regular Position Time Status: Full time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Days (United States of America) Job Description: Job Summary \r\n Responsible for ensuring accuracy, quality, and completeness of clinical documentation to support patient care, regulatory compliance, and appropriate reimbursement. Provides advanced expertise by collaborating with providers, coders, case managers, and the healthcare team to validate severity of illness, risk of mortality, and medical necessity. Conducts comprehensive chart reviews and clarifies provider documentation to improve clinical accuracy and data integrity. Coordinates reporting, trending, and analysis to support organizational quality initiatives and documentation integrity goals. \r\n \r\n Essential Functions \r\n • Performs admission and continued stay reviews to validate principal diagnosis, comorbidities, and clinical indicators supporting severity of illness. \r\n • Conducts follow-up reviews to confirm provider responses and integration of documentation into the medical record. \r\n • Partners with coding specialists to resolve documentation and data discrepancies that impact coding accuracy and reimbursement. \r\n • Develops and maintains data reports, spreadsheets, and dashboards to track trends and outcomes related to documentation integrity. \r\n • Prepares summaries and presentations of review findings and documentation performance for leadership and hospital committees. \r\n • Supports continuous improvement initiatives by identifying gaps in documentation and recommending process enhancements. \r\n • Maintains current knowledge of coding, CDI practices, and regulatory changes to guide accurate documentation review. \r\n • Performs other duties as assigned. \r\n \r\n Education Requirement: Associate’s degree Nursing \r\n \r\n Experience Requirement: 2+ years of related experience \r\n An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. All experience must be paid and in the same related field. Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week. Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted. \r\n \r\n Certifications & Licensures: Registered Nurse \r\n \r\n Working Conditions \r\n A. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs:2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n B. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs:1. Never \r\n C. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs:3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) \r\n D. Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs:2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n E. Sitting at the computer workstation for extended periods:3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) \r\n F. Risk of back injury from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials:2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n G. Repetitive motion:3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time) \r\n H. Working at heights above 4 feet:1. Never \r\n I. Working in confined spaces:1. Never \r\n J. Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job:2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n K. Job-related travel:2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n L. Loud noises:1. Never \r\n M. Temperature extremes:1. Never \r\n N. Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste:2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n O. Radiation:1. Never \r\n P. Burns:1. Never \r\n Q. Cuts/Punctures:2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n R. Bloodborne/airborne pathogens:2. Occasional (< 10% of the time) \r\n S. Recombinant DNA or viral vectors:1. Never \r\n T. Combative/violent people:1. Never \r\n U. Animal handling (including carcasses):1. Never \r\n V. Please specify other(s) and amount of exposure (i.e. Occasional, Intermittent or Regular): N/A \r\n \r\n Physical Demands \r\n This position requires intermittent sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time; performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); intermittent standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; occasional standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds; and occasional lifting, pushing, or pulling objects weighing up to 50 pounds. Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
