    "https://univofky.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/UKSS/job/Joe-Craft-Center/Creative-Producer-Editor_R-000003209-1": {
      "title": "Creative Producer Editor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBeyond Blue Job Posting Title: Creative Producer Editor Requisition Number: R-000003209 Department Name: Creative Content Director Work Location: Joe Craft Center Grade Level: 8 Type of Position: Regular Position Time Status: Full time Equivalency Link https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Shift: Flex (United States of America) Job Description:   Creative Producer Editor    Job Summary   Responsible for creating, producing, and editing high-quality video content that promotes student-athletes, athletic programs, and institutional   initiatives   across digital, social media, and broadcast platforms. Leads all phases of video production, including plan ning, shooting, editing, and content   distribution . Collaborates with internal stakeholders to develop content strategies that support marketing and engagement   objectives   while mentoring student workers and   maintaining   video production equipment and archives.    Essential Functions   •   Conceptualizes, produces, and   delivers   a diverse portfolio of video content, including game recaps, feature stories, promotional videos, and social media assets.    •   Plans, shoots, edits, and distributes video content across multiple   digital   and social media   platforms .   •   Ensures all video content aligns with brand standards, strategic messaging, and organizational goals.   •   Captures high-quality video footage during live events, practices, interviews, and special   activities.     •   Utilizes   audience insights and digital media trends to   optimize   content performance and engagement.    •   Collaborates with coaches, marketing staff, athletic communications personnel, and other departments to   identify   and develop content   opportunities .    •   Participates   in   strategic   planning   discussions   and develops video content strategies that support marketing and   communications objectives .    •   Manages all aspects of video production, including   scriptwriting , scheduling, directing shoots, and overseeing post-production activities.    •   Implements   innovative storytelling and production   techniques   to enhance fan engagement and audience experiences.    •   Mentors, trains, and provides guidance to student workers and interns   regarding   equipment operation, storytelling techniques, and industry best practices.    •   Conducts   instructional   workshops and   training   opportunities   to support student development in video production and content creation.    •   Maintains   vide o   production   equipment and ensures cameras, lighting, audio, and related technologies   remain   operational and up to date.    •   Organizes, archives, and manages video   assets   and metadata to support content retrieval and long-term storage requirements.    •   Monitors   emerging industry trends and technologies and recommends   improvements   that enhance production quality and operational   effectiveness .     • Performs other duties as assigned.   Education Requirement   Bachelor's degree in Video Production, Digital Media, Communications, Journalism, Marketing,   Broadcasting , or   a related   field.    Experience Requirement   2 years of experience   in video production, digital media, content creation, sports media, broadcasting, marketing communications, or   a related   field.    Experience using Adobe Premier Pro, Adobe After Effects, operating cinema cameras, ENG lenses, audio equipment, lighting systems preferred.    An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered.   All experience must be   paid and   in the same related field.   Part-time and PRN experience will be prorated based on hours worked per week.   Volunteer work and internships for academic credit are not counted.   Certifications & Licensures   Valid Driver's License preferred.    Working Conditions   A. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time)   B. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs: 2. Occasional (<10% of the time)   C. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs: 4. Regular (>50% of the time)   D. Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time)   E. Sitting at computer workstation for extended periods: 4. Regular (>50% of the time)   F. Risk of back injury from moving, lifting, or positioning equipment or materials: 2. Occasional (<10% of the time)   G. Repetitive motion: 4. Regular (>50% of the time)   H. Working at heights above 4 feet: 2. Occasional (<10% of the time)   I. Working in confined spaces: 1. Never   J. Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job: 2. Occasional (<10% of the time)   K. Job-related travel: 2. Occasional (<10% of the time)   L. Loud   noises : 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time)   M. Temperature extremes: 2. Occasional (<10% of the time)   N. Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste: 1. Never   O. Radiation: 1. Never   P. Burns: 1. Never   Q. Cuts/Punctures: 2. Occasional (<10% of the time)   R. Bloodborne/airborne pathogens: 1. Never   S. Recombinant DNA or viral vectors: 1. Never   T. Combative/violent people: 1. Never   U. Animal handling (including carcasses): 1. Never   V. Please specify other(s) and amount of exposure ( i.e.   Occasional, Intermittent or Regular): Outdoor athletic event environments and varying weather conditions: 3. Intermittent (10% - 50% of the time)   Physical Demands   This position requires regular standing and walking during athletic events, video shoots, and production activities; regular sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods while editing video content; and regular repetitive hand and arm movements associated with editing software, camera operation, and production equipment. The position requires intermittent lifting, pushing, and pulling of video production equipment and materials weighing up to 50 pounds, occasional setup and breakdown of production equipment, intermittent exposure to loud event environments, and occasional exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Employees must be able to manage multiple projects simultaneously, meet production deadlines, and   maintain   creativity and attention to detail in a fast-paced media environment.     Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.   The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.   Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen."
